    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "GDP Deflator formula: (Nominal GDP / Real GDP) × 100 — frequently asked in inflation and national accounting questions.",
        "Factor Cost = Market Price - Indirect Taxes + Subsidies (FC = MP - NIT).",
        "Real GDP is evaluated at constant base-year prices, making it the true metric for economic growth without inflationary distortions."
      ],
